    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Renewable supplies and reducing fossil dependence",
      "text": "Renewable generation can replace part of fossil energy use where suitable resources, technology and networks are available. It can diversify supply and reduce recurrent purchases of fossil fuel. The size of the contribution depends on actual usable output at the times it is needed. Installed equipment or a maximum rating is not the same as delivered energy, and a growing renewable share does not by itself show that total fossil consumption has fallen.",
