      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-03",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A geothermal resource can provide relatively steady energy where the field is productive and managed suitably. Constraints include exploration risk, drilling and maintenance costs, fluid handling and possible local environmental effects. Extracting heat or fluids faster than a particular system can sustain can reduce its useful performance. The source is renewable in the broader natural-process sense, while an individual project still requires management and monitoring of its resource.",
