    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-04",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Wave energy draws on the movement of surface waves. Devices can convert that motion into mechanical work and electricity. The resource depends on the wave climate, so coastlines differ in suitability. A site requires sufficient usable waves, survivable equipment, maintenance access and a way to deliver power. Being beside the sea does not establish that the resource or the connection costs are suitable for a particular installation.",
