      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Wave systems face a difficult operating environment. Saltwater, storms and moving components create design and repair challenges. Devices may interact with navigation, fishing, habitats or other coastal uses. The relevant judgement compares expected useful energy with cost, reliability and environmental effects. Waves are not tides: surface waves are largely generated by wind, while tidal changes reflect gravitational interactions. Both involve moving seawater but have different timing and technologies.",
