      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Tidal energy uses regular changes or currents associated with tides. A tidal-range system can use a water-level difference, while tidal-stream systems use flowing tidal currents. Suitable range, current speed, seabed and access influence location. Tides are predictable in timing, but generation still varies through the tidal cycle and is not a constant output. A predictable pause is still a period that the supply system must accommodate.",
      "claim_ids": [
