      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-07",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Tidal works can alter sediment movement, habitats or other uses, depending on the design. Strong currents can be useful for energy while also challenging installation and maintenance. A wide coast does not itself establish a suitable range or stream resource. Site-specific measurements and environmental assessment are needed. The explanation should identify the actual energy movement used rather than simply say water makes power.",
