      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Hydroelectric power uses water moving through a height difference to drive turbines connected to generators. River flow supplies water and the usable head provides a vertical energy difference. Some schemes store water in reservoirs; others operate mainly with river flow and limited storage. These designs have different capacity to shift generation through time. Running water is a renewable source, but a station's output can still fall in a dry period.",
