      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Hydroelectric generation can reduce fuel combustion during operation and supply useful electricity where flow, head and infrastructure are suitable. Reservoir designs may allow some control over timing, while run-of-river operation is more directly constrained by current flow. Both need maintenance, transmission and suitable management of river effects. The renewable label does not establish unlimited output or the absence of ecological consequences.",
