      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Solar energy uses incoming radiation. Photovoltaic cells convert light into electricity directly, while solar thermal systems capture heat for uses such as water heating; some larger thermal designs generate electricity through a heat-driven process. These methods should not be merged into a claim that every panel heats water or every solar system drives a turbine. Identify the conversion process shown by the resource.",
