    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Solar photovoltaic output changes with sunlight, cloud, shading and equipment conditions. At night a panel does not provide new sunlight-based generation, so a demand at that time needs storage, another supply or a changed use pattern. Strong sunlight can support a project, but heat, dust, maintenance and connection arrangements also affect useful output. The highest temperature is not automatically the site with the greatest dependable electrical supply.",
      "claim_ids": [
