    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Solar can support distributed services where a suitable system supplies local needs without a long network extension. The design still needs appropriate equipment size, maintenance, affordability and any required storage. A lighting system is not necessarily capable of running cooking equipment or an irrigation pump. Compare the actual load and timing with system capability rather than treating a solar connection as an identical service in every household.",
