    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Biogas is a fuel mixture, including methane, produced when suitable organic material decomposes without oxygen under managed conditions. A digester can use materials such as manure or other appropriate organic residues. The resulting gas can provide heat or power with suitable equipment. A functioning system needs a dependable feedstock, appropriate operating conditions, handling and maintenance. Organic material present somewhere in a district does not automatically become usable gas at a household.",
