    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Biogas can provide an energy use for organic residues and leave material that may have nutrient value when appropriately managed. Benefits depend on the whole system. Gas leakage, unsuitable waste handling or poorly maintained equipment can create risks. Feedstock can also have other uses, while collection requires labour and transport. Assess whether the material supply and practical operation can be maintained rather than assuming that waste means a free unlimited fuel.",
