    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-15",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Wind, although considered separately in siting, is another renewable flow. Turbines extract some energy from moving air and drive a generator. Output varies with wind conditions and turbines have operating limits. The timing of wind generation may complement or coincide with other sources, depending on the actual patterns. A diversified system requires those patterns to be assessed, rather than simply adding several renewable names and assuming a dependable total.",
