    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-16",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A generation-mix comparison distinguishes shares from amounts. Suppose renewable energy rises from twenty to forty units while total supply rises from 100 to 200 units. Its share remains 20% although its amount doubles. If fossil energy simultaneously rises from eighty to 160, total fossil use has grown. Conversely, a rising renewable share can coincide with stable or falling fossil use, depending on total demand. State both numerator and total before describing dependence.",
      "claim_ids": [
