    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A chart of monthly renewable output should show the interval, unit and sources. Compare geothermal, water, solar or other series using matched periods and quantities. A high maximum point does not establish annual dominance; totals require the complete period or suitable aggregation. If the chart has missing observations, do not treat them as zero. The chart's boundaries determine whether a conclusion concerns one station, electricity generation or total national energy.",
