    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-18",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Renewables can improve security by diversifying resources and reducing some imported fuel needs, while also requiring materials, investment and grid services. Storage can move energy to another time, with losses and cost; complementary sources can fill gaps if available; efficient use can reduce the load to be supplied. A realistic plan connects generation to demand, transmission and maintenance instead of judging sources in isolation.",
