    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-20",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Each renewable process has a different physical pathway. In geothermal generation, internal heat drives a suitable conversion system. In wave and tidal systems, moving seawater supplies mechanical energy. In hydroelectricity, flowing water through head turns a turbine. In photovoltaic systems, light is converted directly to electricity. In biogas systems, organic feedstock becomes a combustible gas through managed decomposition. Naming these pathways prevents the generic statement “it turns a turbine” from being used for a photovoltaic panel that has no turbine.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.4.03-1",
