      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-21",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Resource quality can vary within the same broad region. Two coastal sites can have different usable wave conditions or tidal currents; two river sites can have different head; two roofs can have different shading. A large resource map identifies opportunities for closer investigation rather than a final engineering design. Local measurements, access, construction and environmental information are needed before assigning a project a dependable output.",
