      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-22",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A biogas account should specify feedstock and continuity. A digester receiving enough suitable material during one demonstration may not receive it throughout the year. Livestock movement, competing uses or collection difficulties can interrupt the input. A dependable service needs a maintained operating sequence and suitable equipment as well as the biological process. Output should be measured in useful gas or delivered energy over the relevant interval, not inferred solely from the digester's volume.",
