      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-23",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hydroelectric time series illustrates the difference between a renewable resource and a stable output. Suppose monthly generation is twelve, eight and four energy units in three consecutive months as usable flow falls. The three-month total is twenty-four units. Water remains part of a renewing cycle, yet this station's output has declined. Without the rest of the year, the series cannot establish its annual total or prove the same trend will continue indefinitely.",
