      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-24",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Diversification should be tested against coinciding low-output periods. Suppose daylight solar output covers a daytime load, but both solar output and wind fall below an evening load. Listing two technologies does not establish adequacy. A second resource improves reliability only to the extent that its available contribution, storage or other support fills the relevant gap. This is a timing problem that annual energy totals alone can conceal.",
