      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.4.03-25",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Lower dependence on fossil fuels can refer to a smaller share, a smaller absolute quantity or less exposure to imported supply. Those are different objectives. A country can raise domestic renewable production while still importing fossil fuel for growing transport demand. The conclusion needs the sector and measure being assessed. A precise answer can describe a successful electricity contribution without claiming an unmeasured change across the whole energy economy.",
